cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OpenQBW: A pure-Rust reader for QuickBooks QBW backup files"
message: >
  If you use OpenQBW in your research, please cite it using the metadata
  below. Citation is encouraged and appreciated but not legally required.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Riley
    given-names: Nathan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1579-7312"
    website: "https://github.com/Sigilweaver"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sigilweaver/OpenQBW"
url: "https://sigilweaver.app"
abstract: >
  OpenQBW is a standalone, cross-platform reader for Intuit QuickBooks QBW
  backup files, implemented in pure Rust. Python bindings built on PyO3
  integrate with Polars, PyArrow, and Pandas, exposing the QBW page,
  table, and record structures without requiring an Intuit runtime.
license: "Apache-2.0"
license-url: "https://github.com/Sigilweaver/OpenQBW/blob/main/LICENSE"
date-released: "2026-05-31"
version: "0.1.0"
keywords:
  - QBW
  - QuickBooks
  - Intuit
  - file format
  - parser
  - Apache Arrow
  - Rust
  - Python
